From 089c31f9a763bbf9e708d51865bf89a9ea5e748a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 10BE Software UG <support@ns.10be.de>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 21:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Allow 10BE CarbCam to prefill the Treatments carb entry
 screen

Adds a small URL-scheme entry point that lets 10BE CarbCam
(package de.be10.carbcam) hand its carb estimate over to Trio.
On URL receipt the Treatments screen opens prefilled with the
supplied carb / fat / protein / notes values; the user must
still confirm via the standard Save and continue button before
anything is written to CoreData.

Design notes:

  * URL scheme: carbcam-trio://
  * URL format: carbcam-trio://carbs?value=N&fat=N&protein=N
                                    &notes=...&source=...
  * Validation: value 1..80 g (required), fat 0..80 g (optional),
    protein 0..80 g (optional), notes max 200 chars. Out-of-range
    values are silently rejected.
  * No caller identity check is performed: anyone can open the
    URL, but the user always confirms in the Treatments screen
    before logging.
  * No silent CoreData writes, no silent bolusing. All existing
    confirmation flows are unchanged.
  * fat and protein are passed as separate URL parameters so
    Trio's existing UI fields can be prefilled directly without
    FPU-style 50/50 splitting heuristics.

Implementation:

  * TrioApp.handleURL gains a `carbs` host case and a small
    handleCarbCamURL helper.
  * A new ExternalCarbsPrefill enum acts as a one-shot prefill
    carrier (store / consume / hasValue). consume() clears the
    value as it returns, so a later manual re-open of the
    Treatments screen does not re-apply the same prefill.
  * Home.StateModel listens for the .openAddCarbsFromCarbCam
    notification via Combine and calls showModal(for: .treatmentView),
    the same route the "+" button in the tab bar already uses.
    A cold-start check covers the case where the URL arrives
    before subscribe() has run.
  * Treatments.StateModel.setupSettings() consumes the prefill at
    the end of its existing initialization, clamping each value
    against the corresponding max setting. saveMeal() clamps again
    before storing, so the limits hold either way.

Adapted from the original patch by 10BE Software UG (2 Jun 2026),
which targeted the AddCarbs module. That module is no longer part
of the Trio Xcode project: AddCarbsStateModel.swift and
AddCarbsRootView.swift remain on disk but have no reference in
project.pbxproj, and the `enum AddCarbs` namespace they extend was
removed along with AddCarbsDataFlow.swift. The original patch
therefore applies cleanly with git apply and then fails to build
with "cannot find 'AddCarbs' in scope" in HomeRootView.swift.
Carb entry now lives in the Treatments module, so this version
routes there instead and drops the HomeRootView sheet entirely.

Target branch: nightscout/Trio main
